ntfs-3g (ntfs-macos) patch 0011: ntfs_possible_symlink() checks the attribute length before it reads the tag

Rationale (T-M3-25, ADR-026, finding F4, GHSA-vp2x-xjmj-x4x2, tests/fuzz/TRIAGE.md): in NTFS-3G 2026.9.28,
libntfs-3g/reparse.c ntfs_possible_symlink() guards with "reparse_attr && attr_size" (line 927) and then
reads reparse_attr->reparse_tag (line 928), 4 bytes at offset 0. A $REPARSE_POINT attribute of 1 to 3
bytes makes the read run past the allocation of ntfs_attr_readall() (line 925). The function is called by
ntfs_dir_entry_type() (dir.c:923), from ntfs_filldir() during ntfs_readdir(), for every directory entry
whose file has the reparse flag, so a plain "ls" of a crafted volume reaches it. With ASan the ntfs-3g
daemon exits with status 1 during that listing; valgrind shows a use of uninitialised memory at
reparse.c:928.
Change (libntfs-3g/reparse.c, one hunk): the tag is read only when
attr_size >= (s64)sizeof(REPARSE_POINT), the same header test valid_reparse_data() makes (the structure
is packed and reparse_data[] has size zero, so this equals offsetof(REPARSE_POINT, reparse_data); sizeof
is used because reparse.c does not otherwise include stddef.h). The buffer is now freed whenever it was
allocated: before, an attribute with attr_size == 0 returned a non-NULL buffer that was never freed (a
leak of the empty allocation); with the restructured test free() sits after the size test.
Checked in reparse.c, same pattern (reads reparse_tag or the header of data read from disk without a size
test): none found beyond this function.
  - ntfs_make_symlink() (line 814 to 817): reads only after valid_reparse_data(), which tests
    size >= sizeof(REPARSE_POINT) first. Safe.
  - ntfs_get_reparse_point() (line 1445): returns the buffer only after valid_reparse_data(). Safe; its
    callers (wsl_getattr() and ntfs_reparse_check_wsl() in src/ntfs-3g.c, ntfs-3g_common.c) get a
    validated buffer.
  - ntfs_reparse_check_wsl() (line 447): reads the tag of the buffer it is given; every caller passes
    the result of ntfs_get_reparse_point(). Safe.
  - ntfs_get_ntfs_reparse_data() (line 1174): copies attr_size bytes to the caller and reads no field.
    Safe.
  - remove_reparse_index() (line 1000): ntfs_attr_pread(na, 0, 4, ...) and a "size == 4" test before the
    tag is used. Safe.
  - set_reparse_data() (line 1100): value comes from ntfs_set_ntfs_reparse_data(), which calls
    valid_reparse_data() first (line 1213). Safe.
  - ntfsprogs/ntfsinfo.c (line 2167) reads a reparse attribute for printing; it is a command line tool,
    not built or shipped by ntfs-macos, and is not patched.
Scope: library-wide and cross-platform (no __APPLE__ guard). It only adds a rejection of a malformed
on-disk attribute (a reparse attribute shorter than its 8-byte header is never a symlink).
Upstream status: reported privately 2026-11-16 as GHSA-vp2x-xjmj-x4x2; carried until a fixed NTFS-3G release
is pinned, then removed (ADR-026).
A reader of the same tag outside reparse.c, ntfs_inode_sync_file_name() in inode.c, is fixed by patch 0013.
Test: ctest fuzz.findings.F4 replays tests/fuzz/image/findings/F4-possible-symlink-heap-overflow.bin through
fuzz_replay_mountwalk (directory reads on), registered only for an ASan build. Verified in Environment A: it
fails on the unpatched library (heap-buffer-overflow at reparse.c) and passes with the patch, in clang and
gcc builds at -O0 and -O1, with and without UBSan. Standalone image: mount and "ls -laR" under valgrind
(ntfs-3g): conditional jump on uninitialised memory at reparse.c:928 unpatched, none patched.

--- a/libntfs-3g/reparse.c
+++ b/libntfs-3g/reparse.c
@@ -924,13 +924,16 @@
 	possible = FALSE;
 	reparse_attr = (REPARSE_POINT*)ntfs_attr_readall(ni,
 			AT_REPARSE_POINT,(ntfschar*)NULL, 0, &attr_size);
-	if (reparse_attr && attr_size) {
-		switch (reparse_attr->reparse_tag) {
-		case IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT :
-		case IO_REPARSE_TAG_SYMLINK :
-		case IO_REPARSE_TAG_LX_SYMLINK :
-			possible = TRUE;
-		default : ;
+	if (reparse_attr) {
+			/* the tag is read only from a complete header */
+		if (attr_size >= (s64)sizeof(REPARSE_POINT)) {
+			switch (reparse_attr->reparse_tag) {
+			case IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT :
+			case IO_REPARSE_TAG_SYMLINK :
+			case IO_REPARSE_TAG_LX_SYMLINK :
+				possible = TRUE;
+			default : ;
+			}
 		}
 		free(reparse_attr);
 	}
